data: {"type":"streamAssistantItem","item":"event","value":{"event":"end","part":0,"content":{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Engaging with new lore**\n\nIâm thinking we have new lore and some prior context to work with. I should briefly engage by noting that the separation could mean the guild is dependent on miners, which could provide potential leverage during storms. I wonder if blue salt is scarce and what lenses do. I shouldnât invent details, though. Mentioning something like, âThat gives Vesper's beacon a supply chainâ might be good, but I want to emphasize there's no ownership involved. I'd also ask who controls mining and what that relationship looks like.","native":{"item":{"reasoning":"**Engaging with new lore**\n\nIâm thinking we have new lore and some prior context to work with. I should briefly engage by noting that the separation could mean the guild is dependent on miners, which could provide potential leverage during storms. I wonder if blue salt is scarce and what lenses do. I shouldnât invent details, though. Mentioning something like, âThat gives Vesper's beacon a supply chainâ might be good, but I want to emphasize there's no ownership involved. I'd also ask who controls mining and what that relationship looks like.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"**Engaging with new lore**\n\nIâm thinking we have new lore and some prior context to work with. I should briefly engage by noting that the separation could mean the guild is dependent on miners, which could provide potential leverage during storms. I wonder if blue salt is scarce and what lenses do. I shouldnât invent details, though. Mentioning something like, âThat gives Vesper's beacon a supply chainâ might be good, but I want to emphasize there's no ownership involved. I'd also ask who controls mining and what that relationship looks like.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq4yIlxTifLl7zYHdICD7i